sted scope bullet therefore changes the identity, and core.js:382 returns the fresh subject. current-waivers.test.js:109 and 160-169 assert this and passed on 8874fd9 (shard 1 ok 3, shard 2 ok 4).","id":"codex/review-light-brief-indentation","status":"resolved"},{"evidence":"Reconsidered because briefScope was rewritten. briefScopeChanged (delegation.js:433-439) and assertBriefScopeUnchanged (443-447) call the same indentation-preserving briefScope, so a promoted nested scope bullet makes before !== after and the run hands back (core.js:572, and 461 for a human re-authorization). The delegation suite passed on 8874fd9 (1a1189f9…, 17/17, including the light delegation scope-change hand-back tests). PROTOCOL.md:84-88 states that the same comparison decides a delegated hand-back.","id":"codex/review-delegated-brief-indentation","status":"resolved"},{"evidence":"Carried forward because the code is unchanged this round. autonomous.js:105-106 passingGate rejects a PASS that carries waivedCoverage, and allowedRunOutcome is built on it. delegation.js:467 (delegated acceptance, 'no exceptions') and core.js:1192/1198 still use allowedRunOutcome. The unit test at current-waivers.test.js:81-87 passed on 8874fd9 (shard 1 ok 2).","id":"claude-code/F1","status":"resolved"},{"evidence":"Carried forward because the code is unchanged this round. authorization.js:177 requires passingGate for every required outcome. current-waivers.test.js:89-104 (standing grant, verification waived without accept, authorization.apply rejected, no accept recorded) passed on 8874fd9 (shard 2 ok 2).","id":"claude-code/F3","status":"resolved"}],"findings":[{"blocking":false,"classId":"brief-scope-semantic-whitespace","classStatement":"Whitespace normalization treats some code that Markdown renders verbatim as collapsible prose in the light-brief comparison.","criterion":"R4","evidence":"FENCE at delegation.js:319 (/^ {0,3}(`{3,}|~{3,})/u) recognises fences only with zero to three leading spaces and has no