ers:77 passed (shard 1 ok 1)."},"mandateAssessment":{"evidence":"Goal: #145 items 1-3 are delivered in one change set:\n- the waiver past coverage is recorded honestly (core.js:1136-1186 waivedCoverage, the decision's observed outcomes, the explainer);\n- the findings log grows without re-authorization (core.js:375-384 with delegation.js briefScope);\n- run.start writes featureBaseSha (workspace.js).\n\nConstraint 1: the reviewer pipeline is untouched. Constraint 2: no public PR or issue text is in the evidence, and source and doc comments cite only 'GitHub issue #145' with no local paths or other project names; local paths appear only in runner receipt metadata. Constraint 3: nothing performs or authorizes a merge, and unattended merge is tightened (actions.js:162/195).\n\nAuthority is human-confirmed ('Proceed' on the fixed mandate).","outcome":"PASS"},"outcome":"PASS","summary":"This is the round 4 review (band high-and-medium-regressions) of the complete FEATURE change: head 8874fd9 against base and target e59b02c. It passes.\n\nThe one open finding, codex/review-light-brief-semantic-whitespace (high), is fixed in the source. briefLines (delegation.js:320-330) now marks fence-opening, fenced and closing lines as code. briefScope (350-364) keeps those lines verbatim behind a \\u0000 prefix, blank ones included. proseWithSpans (333-349) keeps inline code spans verbatim. Prose still collapses inner and trailing whitespace and drops blank lines, and leading indentation still counts. The implementer's claim is confirmed by the source and by the new assertions at current-waivers.test.js:106-116, which passed on 8874fd9 (receipt c4a51d75…, shard 1 ok 3).\n\nThe two indentation fixes that this rewrite touches still hold: codex/review-light-brief-indentation and codex/review-delegated-brief-indentation. claude-code/F1 and F3 are carried forward because autonomous.js, authorization.js and core.js are not in this round's regression paths, and passingGate and allowedRunOutcome are still used at every unattended-authority site.\n\nI found one low, non-blocking finding. It is another instance of the semantic-whitespace class: code that Markdown treats as code but FENCE does not recognise, namely indented code blocks and fences indented four or more spaces inside nested list items. Inner whitespace there is still collapsed. Triggering it needs an unusual combination of conditions, and it is still stricter than the base rule ('Whitespace-only differences are ignored') that the approved design reused.\n\nCaveats:\n- The full `npm test --prefix cli` suite has not been observed. It rests on the planned required hosted CI jobs 'Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 acceptance', which run ci/portable-acceptance.sh:21. Acceptance in this hosted-CI repository enforces this unless a human waives verification (core.js:1176-1186).\n- No changed-path list was supplied. I took the paths from roundPolicy.regressionPaths, the prior PASS report's coverage and direct inspection.\n- No PR or issue text is in the evidence."}]}